# V1b (SOFT, card M only): the V5 single-card byte gate at FULL scope, copied from tp4-v5split-jobs V1b: selftest, every regime (R1 x5 seeds, R2, R3, R3b, RA, the 2,048-token R4 chain, R5 real text on layers 0, 23 and 47), users 1-3, the two negative controls, the stale-input sequence,
# 100 traced replays with the inputs restaged in place, the program-cache deltas and the timing arms. Four users x 16 rows, K5-A against V5 bit for bit on raw page images. A full-scope PASS prints the sha256 triple (v5_triple) that gdn_seq_block_split.QUALIFIED takes: commit it
# (one line) on a later commit and V5 can then be gated on four cards; until then the flag refuses, and W2 is measured without it. The timing label (proceed at V - A <= -65 us) is informative: the byte verdict is the gate.
# READ: 'GDN_V5 verdict=PASS scope=full ...' and the last JSON line. FAIL with 'bytes>0' is a real difference; NO-DECISION is not a pass. Skipped if V1a read a watcher error, a hang or a FAIL. Duration (estimate): 60-120 min (container timeout 3 h; the per-call watchdog exits 3 on a hang, then reset the target card only).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the card is resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# CARD M ONLY, BEFORE ANY QUAD JOB: the cardm step runs one board; it never runs while a quad step holds the cards, and the harness refuses while anything else can reach the board.
# The harness's container turns the image's C2 boot hook off (QWEN_C2_SERVING=0) and unsets the baked four-card mesh descriptor (env -u TT_MESH_GRAPH_DESC_PATH); the workflow's
# cardm step waits for other CI's buildx builders instead of refusing the window. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1 is the image B0 built (a harness mounts this checkout's scripts, so any current C2 image carries the runtime it needs).
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/v5split/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2-1
